  "explicit_limitations": [
    "Offline clustering uses historical ground-truth output length L whereas online admission uses Clairvoyant's 3-class proxy L_hat; class token boundaries, representative lengths, Clairvoyant accuracy on the 5 traces, oracle-L vs L_hat error ablation, and drift re-clustering are absent.",
    "Table 2 normalizes latencies to 10x/5x of Naive's 0.1 req/s P90 and compares all methods at Naive's saturation req/s; raw latencies (ms/s) and per-method maximum sustainable req/s are unprinted outside Hybrid load sweeps.",
    "Section 4.4 compares Dynamo's static effective-ISL and ratio rules only (global threshold constants unprinted) and explicitly excludes Dynamo's load-based policies.",
    "Single-regime workloads show no simultaneous improvement over Dynamo/Naive: ArXiv P2D2 reaches 1.03/0.24 vs Naive 1.00/0.22, L-Eval swaps TTFT vs TPOT across P3D1/P2D2, and all 4 methods exceed 1.0 TPOT (1.01-1.06) on HumanEval.",
    "Each policy table binds to a fixed P/D allocation (P3D1 or P2D2); evaluation covers a single model (Qwen3.8-72B on 4xH20-SXM nodes), Algorithm 1's Span(P_c) > tau check is undefined in prose, and no code repository is linked."
  ],
